/**
 * DDAM logo mark.
 *
 * Auto-traced from `~/Downloads/Company logo/logo-white.png` with potrace
 * (alpha channel, 6x upscale, gaussian-smoothed before thresholding to remove
 * the source PNG's aliasing). Regenerate with `scripts/trace-logo.py` if the
 * artwork changes — or just paste the official vector's paths into LOGO_PATHS.
 *
 * The mark renders three ways:
 *   <LogoMark />               the whole thing, self-contained
 *   <LogoSprite id="x" />      hidden <defs> copy, so the path data ships once
 *   <LogoHalf spriteId="x" />  a <use> of that sprite, for the split animation
 *
 * Nothing here assumes the mark is symmetric or knows where its "halves" are —
 * the launch animation cuts it down the middle with a CSS clip-path, so this
 * all keeps working if you swap in different artwork.
 */

